# Wave W17-O (Ragged Pass): stair sand — broken-stair sand: pale sand with the stair’s stepped lip edges drawn in the kind itself — two worn stone lips cross every tile, dark tread-line over a pale scuffed riser (design-authorised: a clear connected path of pale sand running end to end, Mt. Smokestack down to Steamspring; the design’s cut stair flights are drawn in the path kind’s own art, the fallfloor discipline). The only stepped path in the fleet — split from every flat sand by its lips.
